From 100066564a7f875d736563419f03916eeedcbccd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Sturla <rsturla@redhat.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:25:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve toolchain paths through compiler symlinks

### Motivation

SwiftPM assumes that sibling tools and resources are installed relative to the path used to invoke the Swift compiler. This breaks when a public compiler path, such as /usr/bin/swiftc, is a symlink into a complete toolchain under another prefix. Lookup can then miss the selected toolchain or use an unrelated system tool.

### Modifications

Resolve the selected compiler before deriving paths owned by its toolchain. Search the resolved compiler directory before the public directory while preserving configured toolset order and the public path as a fallback.

Use these paths for adjacent tools, the Swift interpreter, plug-in tool searches, SwiftPM configuration and libraries, host SDK tools, index-store loading, and Linux compiler-owned resources. Derive the Swift Build toolchain path from a resolved <prefix>/bin layout while preserving the existing /usr and /usr/local behavior.

### Result

SwiftPM uses tools and resources from the installation that owns the selected compiler. Existing non-symlinked, /usr, and /usr/local layouts keep their current behavior.
